? Why does BFS find shortest paths in an unweighted graph?
- It tries every possible path
- It always moves towards the target
+ It reaches vertices in order of distance
- It uses a priority queue
> The queue processes all vertices at distance d before any at distance d + 1, so the first visit is along a shortest path.

? A road network has 1,000,000 junctions and about 2,500,000 roads. Which representation?
- an adjacency matrix
+ adjacency lists
- an edge list only
- a binary heap
> A matrix would need 10^12 entries; adjacency lists need memory proportional to V + E.

? When should BFS mark a vertex as visited?
- When it is popped from the queue
- After all its neighbours are processed
+ When it is pushed onto the queue
- It does not need to
> Marking on push stops the same vertex being queued several times.
